{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"normal","reason":"The default gate profile causes a reproduced repository test failure, making affected gates reject valid changes."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Gate code can read Cargo registry credentials when the owner has stored a token in the standard Cargo home."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"secret","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An editor can read credentials relocated through supported environment variables unless the owner adds an explicit denial."},{"id":"F4","consequence":"secret","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Loading a second configuration in the same daemon process removes the first configuration's custom credential protections, though no current production path doing so was identified."},{"id":"F5","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A future removal of the final private-path denial could escape the existing tests, while the current runtime rule remains present."},{"id":"F6","consequence":"test","trigger":"plausible","reason":"The tests fail because of their setup when run in a linked worktree or with a nonexistent Codex home."}]}